          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2>\n<h3 id=\"bluemira-is-an-integrated-inter-disciplinary-design-tool-for-future-fusion-reactors-it-incorporates-several-modules-to-carry-out-a-range-of-typical-conceptual-fusion-reactor-design-activities\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Fusion-Power-Plant-Framework/bluemira\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><code>Bluemira</code></a> is an integrated inter-disciplinary design tool for future fusion reactors. It incorporates several modules to carry out a range of typical conceptual fusion reactor design activities.</h3>\n<h4 id=\"this-notebook-uses-our-spherical-tokamak-example\">This notebook uses our <a href=\"https://github.com/Fusion-Power-Plant-Framework/bluemira-spherical-tokamak\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Spherical Tokamak example</a>.</h4>\n<h4 id=\"if-youd-like-to-learn-more-about-bluemira-head-to-our-github-repo-andor-read-our-nuclear-fusion-paper\">If you'd like to learn more about <code>bluemira</code>, head to our <a href=\"https://github.com/Fusion-Power-Plant-Framework/bluemira\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo</a> and/or read our <a href=\"https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1741-4326/aea584\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Nuclear Fusion paper</a>.</h4></span>"
          }
